[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186073914 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-889c45f8-a956-5ef6-ac2b-6cd191ad30dc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-889c45f8-a956-5ef6-ac2b-6cd191ad30dc" :question/id #uuid "889c45f8-a956-5ef6-ac2b-6cd191ad30dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-53664" :question/problem "![](images/01/01b6ade0a9b4945c0381848092e9b2289f823c49b2c5c138a29187e7f541787c.png)\n\nThe two pentagons shown above are similar. What is the correct similarity statement?" :question/worked-solution "Since, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∠A≅∠U,\\,∠B≅∠V,\\,∠C≅∠W,\\,∠D≅∠X,\\,∠E≅∠Y,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n- $A$ corresponds to $U,$\n\n- $B$ corresponds to $V,$\n\n- $C$ corresponds to $W,$\n\n- $D$ corresponds to $X,$\n\n- $E$ corresponds to $Y.$\n\nTherefore, $ABCDE∼UVWXY.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3086ccfe-34d4-5016-955b-04dc749a45e1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3086ccfe-34d4-5016-955b-04dc749a45e1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3086ccfe-34d4-5016-955b-04dc749a45e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e831d608-ab95-5cb5-bd60-e9a515a2274f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e831d608-ab95-5cb5-bd60-e9a515a2274f" "answer-f074f9a2-1f24-594d-a3e3-1978813ac002" "answer-f496cc6b-a69d-5e9f-b778-efe587c3fac0" "answer-0560459a-bce6-5338-82e7-960929cfc752" "answer-3d8bb24e-348f-5983-913d-51ca2226f57e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e831d608-ab95-5cb5-bd60-e9a515a2274f" :answer/id #uuid "e831d608-ab95-5cb5-bd60-e9a515a2274f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "ABCDE∼UVWXY" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f074f9a2-1f24-594d-a3e3-1978813ac002" :answer/id #uuid "f074f9a2-1f24-594d-a3e3-1978813ac002" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "ABCDE∼UYXWV" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f496cc6b-a69d-5e9f-b778-efe587c3fac0" :answer/id #uuid "f496cc6b-a69d-5e9f-b778-efe587c3fac0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "ABCDE∼YUVWX" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0560459a-bce6-5338-82e7-960929cfc752" :answer/id #uuid "0560459a-bce6-5338-82e7-960929cfc752" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "EABCD∼XYUVW" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d8bb24e-348f-5983-913d-51ca2226f57e" :answer/id #uuid "3d8bb24e-348f-5983-913d-51ca2226f57e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "EABCD∼YUVXW" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186074218 :question/problem "Given that $△ABC∼△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′},$ $AB=4\\,cm$ and $BC=6\\,cm,$\nwhich of the following could be the values of ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}{C}^{′}?$\n\nI. ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}=16\\,cm,\\,{B}^{′}{C}^{′}=24\\,cm$\n\nII. ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}=20\\,cm,\\,{B}^{′}{C}^{′}=30\\,cm$\n\nIII. ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}=32\\,cm,\\,{B}^{′}{C}^{′}=42\\,cm$" :question/worked-solution "For similar polygons, the ratios of lengths of the corresponding sides should be the same.\n\n- Let's check for this in option I:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{AB}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}} & =\\frac{4}{16}=\\frac{1}{4}, \\\\ \\frac{BC}{{B}^{′}{C}^{′}} & =\\frac{6}{24}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, option I does give possible values of ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}{C}^{′}.$\n\n- For option II, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{AB}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}} & =\\frac{4}{20}=\\frac{1}{5}, \\\\ \\frac{BC}{{B}^{′}{C}^{′}} & =\\frac{6}{30}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, option II does give possible values of ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}{C}^{′}.$\n\n- For option III, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{AB}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}} & =\\frac{4}{32}=\\frac{1}{8}, \\\\ \\frac{BC}{{B}^{′}{C}^{′}} & =\\frac{6}{42}=\\frac{1}{7}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, option III does not give possible values of ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}{C}^{′}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186071546 :answer-field/correct 17592186071548 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073913 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5a648c7b-b62d-5742-8e25-e411a6e50067"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5a648c7b-b62d-5742-8e25-e411a6e50067" :question/id #uuid "5a648c7b-b62d-5742-8e25-e411a6e50067" :question/math-academy-id "q-88002" :question/problem "![](images/99/99212835e0eec95ac4ebd0c7d0fd49e1bb7e1a392f53251aa49510ac8ef5b65d.png)\n\nWhich of the above quadrilaterals are similar to $T$ (other than $T$ itself)?" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $T$ is a right trapezoid with one pair of parallel opposite sides.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given polygons.\n\n- $K$ is *not* similar to $T.$ The polygon $K$ is a right trapezoid, and the corresponding angles are congruent, but the ratios of the lengths of the corresponding sides are not the same: \n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{14}\\ne \\frac{6}{6}\n$$\n\n- $R$ is *not* similar to $T$ because $R$ is not a trapezoid (it's a rectangle since it has $2$ pairs of opposite parallel sides, and $2$ pairs of right angles).\n\n- $M$ is similar to $T.$ Indeed, $M$ is a right trapezoid. Furthermore, the corresponding angles are congruent, and the ratios of the lengths of the corresponding sides are the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{14}=\\frac{3}{6}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$M$ only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-865551b8-c0d8-5cf9-868e-7a602dfa6e44"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-865551b8-c0d8-5cf9-868e-7a602dfa6e44" :answer-field/id #uuid "865551b8-c0d8-5cf9-868e-7a602dfa6e44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-54e63c6d-254e-54cc-8466-5d5bf3d74155" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c0715756-6c47-5bbc-ac2f-30e9b24661cd" "answer-5bdfd74e-ff63-5abb-9563-5fa157d583fd" "answer-8419996f-9e9b-515d-b6eb-d75dfba8906e" "answer-54e63c6d-254e-54cc-8466-5d5bf3d74155" "answer-3c8c637f-7506-5929-a813-aedf842eb2f5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0715756-6c47-5bbc-ac2f-30e9b24661cd" :answer/id #uuid "c0715756-6c47-5bbc-ac2f-30e9b24661cd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$K$ and $M$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5bdfd74e-ff63-5abb-9563-5fa157d583fd" :answer/id #uuid "5bdfd74e-ff63-5abb-9563-5fa157d583fd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$K$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8419996f-9e9b-515d-b6eb-d75dfba8906e" :answer/id #uuid "8419996f-9e9b-515d-b6eb-d75dfba8906e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$M$ and $R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54e63c6d-254e-54cc-8466-5d5bf3d74155" :answer/id #uuid "54e63c6d-254e-54cc-8466-5d5bf3d74155" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$M$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c8c637f-7506-5929-a813-aedf842eb2f5" :answer/id #uuid "3c8c637f-7506-5929-a813-aedf842eb2f5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-d340a7ac-67ef-5612-b337-ffb063b5d526" :activity/id #uuid "d340a7ac-67ef-5612-b337-ffb063b5d526" :activity/title "Similarity and Similar Polygons" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049112 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-9a482e98-3882-5312-9956-5490d87f2d07" "step-4f04fdc1-79b6-5d81-b085-c044626bc257" "step-a8d4dd43-e6fc-58cb-b0ab-de5e3f09f025"] :activity/first-step "step-9a482e98-3882-5312-9956-5490d87f2d07" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-9a482e98-3882-5312-9956-5490d87f2d07" :step/id #uuid "9a482e98-3882-5312-9956-5490d87f2d07" :step/content "question-889c45f8-a956-5ef6-ac2b-6cd191ad30dc" :step/next "step-4f04fdc1-79b6-5d81-b085-c044626bc257" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4f04fdc1-79b6-5d81-b085-c044626bc257" :step/id #u