\n\nI. ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}=16\\,cm,\\,{B}^{′}{C}^{′}=24\\,cm$\n\nII. ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}=20\\,cm,\\,{B}^{′}{C}^{′}=30\\,cm$\n\nIII. ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}=32\\,cm,\\,{B}^{′}{C}^{′}=42\\,cm$"] [17592186074218 :question/worked-solution "For similar polygons, the ratios of lengths of the corresponding sides should be the same.\n\n- Let's check for this in option I:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{AB}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}} & =\\frac{4}{16}=\\frac{1}{4}, \\\\ \\frac{BC}{{B}^{′}{C}^{′}} & =\\frac{6}{24}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, option I does give possible values of ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}{C}^{′}.$\n\n- For option II, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{AB}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}} & =\\frac{4}{20}=\\frac{1}{5}, \\\\ \\frac{BC}{{B}^{′}{C}^{′}} & =\\frac{6}{30}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, option II does give possible values of ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}{C}^{′}.$\n\n- For option III, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{AB}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}} & =\\frac{4}{32}=\\frac{1}{8}, \\\\ \\frac{BC}{{B}^{′}{C}^{′}} & =\\frac{6}{42}=\\frac{1}{7}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, option III does not give possible values of ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}{C}^{′}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""] [17592186074218 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [17592186071546 :answer-field/correct 17592186071548] ["question-5a648c7b-b62d-5742-8e25-e411a6e50067" :question/id #uuid "5a648c7b-b62d-5742-8e25-e411a6e50067"] ["question-5a648c7b-b62d-5742-8e25-e411a6e50067" :question/math-academy-id "q-88002"] ["question-5a648c7b-b62d-5742-8e25-e411a6e50067" :question/problem "![](images/99/99212835e0eec95ac4ebd0c7d0fd49e1bb7e1a392f53251aa49510ac8ef5b65d.png)\n\nWhich of the above quadrilaterals are similar to $T$ (other than $T$ itself)?"] ["question-5a648c7b-b62d-5742-8e25-e411a6e50067" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $T$ is a right trapezoid with one pair of parallel opposite sides.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given polygons.\n\n- $K$ is *not* similar to $T.$ The polygon $K$ is a right trapezoid, and the corresponding angles are congruent, but the ratios of the lengths of the corresponding sides are not the same: \n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{14}\\ne \\frac{6}{6}\n$$\n\n- $R$ is *not* similar to $T$ because $R$ is not a trapezoid (it's a rectangle since it has $2$ pairs of opposite parallel sides, and $2$ pairs of right angles).\n\n- $M$ is similar to $T.$ Indeed, $M$ is a right trapezoid. Furthermore, the corresponding angles are congruent, and the ratios of the lengths of the corresponding sides are the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{14}=\\frac{3}{6}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$M$ only\"."] ["question-5a648c7b-b62d-5742-8e25-e411a6e50067" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-865551b8-c0d8-5cf9-868e-7a602dfa6e44" :answer-field/id #uuid "865551b8-c0d8-5cf9-868e-7a602dfa6e44"] ["answer-c0715756-6c47-5bbc-ac2f-30e9b24661cd" :answer/id #uuid "c0715756-6c47-5bbc-ac2f-30e9b24661cd"] ["answer-c0715756-6c47-5bbc-ac2f-30e9b24661cd" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-c0715756-6c47-5bbc-ac2f-30e9b24661cd" :answer/value "$K$ and $M$ only"] ["answer-5bdfd74e-ff63-5abb-9563-5fa157d583fd" :answer/id #uuid "5bdfd74e-ff63-5abb-9563-5fa157d583fd"] ["answer-5bdfd74e-ff63-5abb-9563-5fa157d583fd" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-5bdfd74e-ff63-5abb-9563-5fa157d583fd" :answer/value "$K$ only"] ["answer-8419996f-9e9b-515d-b6eb-d75dfba8906e" :answer/id #uuid "8419996f-9e9b-515d-b6eb-d75dfba8906e"] ["answer-8419996f-9e9b-515d-b6eb-d75dfba8906e" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-8419996f-9e9b-515d-b6eb-d75dfba8906e" :answer/value "$M$ and $R$ only"] ["answer-54e63c6d-254e-54cc-8466-5d5bf3d74155" :answer/id #uuid "54e63c6d-254e-54cc-8466-5d5bf3d74155"] ["answer-54e63c6d-254e-54cc-8466-5d5bf3d74155" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-54e63c6d-254e-54cc-8466-5d5bf3d74155" :answer/value "$M$ only"] ["answer-3c8c637f-7506-5929-a813-aedf842eb2f5" :answer/id #uuid "3c8c637f